Z||000000||Johnson's85SE||03-22-2001||12:10 PM||||I went and got the steering wheel remover tool. Took off the clip, Took off the main bolt, then screwed in the two steering wheel lock screws, then started to screw in the middle screw. I was screwing till I thought I would bust the steering wheel. Is there some trick? To get her off (The car, not what you are thinking)? She is an 1985 Fiero, Manual tran. Am I missing some step? Please Advise, I only have one night left on the rental. Thanks, Chris<P>------------------<BR>If it isn't broke, it's not my car.||||reg||13
Z||000001||deceler8||03-22-2001||01:01 PM||||While you have everything apart, take the horn button off your steering wheel and check the tightness of the six screws that hold the wheel onto the hub...they're torx screws and if they're loose, you'll get some sloppiness in steering.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||03-22-2001||06:18 PM||||Just keep going, It should feel really tough and then it will pop off.  It will feel like it is breaking something, but it's not.  The spline is very tight on the wheel.  It should be easier putting the new one on.||||reg||1
